+# No-Go Discipline Checklist
+
+## Exact bounded sentence
+
+> The enumerated current structural premises do not select the Wilson
+> same-slot point on the supplied carrier.
+
+This is a current-premise counterfamily statement. It is not a universal
+impossibility claim, not a claim that no future law can select the point, and
+not a claim that an axiom amendment is required.
+
+## N1 — Alternative route enumeration
+
+The families below differ in primary object, mechanism, or terminal
+obligation under the proof-search governance tuple.
+
+| Family | Marker | Attempt and terminal result | Evidence |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Same-operator coefficient reconstruction | `ATTEMPTED` | Put canonical electric and magnetic forms in one self-adjoint Hamiltonian and ask whether the named structural predicates fix their ratio. The exact family `H_g=g^2H_E+g^-2H_B` survives for every `g>0`, so those predicates do not fix the ratio. | Source note Theorem H1 and the primary runner's exact coefficient controls. |
+| Invariant-effect selection | `ATTEMPTED` | Ask gauge covariance to choose the binary registration effect. Schur decomposition gives the full square `aP_3+bP_1`; sharpness is an additional condition. | Source note Theorem E1 and commutant/effect checks. |
+| Repeatable-instrument selection | `ATTEMPTED` | Fix the sharp `P_3/P_1` effects, then ask covariance and repeatability to choose the state update. The explicit `lambda` family supplies distinct CP, complete, covariant, repeatable maps. | Source note Theorem I1 and Choi/covariance/purity checks. |
+| Exact same-carrier electric/magnetic duality | `ATTEMPTED` | Try to force equal coefficients through a unitary or antiunitary exchange of the raw electric and magnetic operators. The unbounded Casimir and bounded Wilson multiplier cannot be conjugate. | Source note Theorem D1 and Casimir/center controls. |
+| Identity-tangent fluctuation law | `ATTEMPTED` | Ask an independently fixed one-tick kernel law to set the canonical negative log-Hessian. This route succeeds conditionally: `-Hess_e log K_tick=g_can` implies `beta=2N_c`; the campaign did not derive the law. | Source note Theorem W1 and independently evaluated matrix Hessians. |
+| Minimal-axiom/Record rate selection | `RULED OUT BY PRIOR` for the named foundation alone | Ask Admissibility or Record to supply the Hamiltonian, step rate, or normalization. The approved foundation explicitly withholds Hamiltonians, transition weights, dynamics, source/action, and `g_bare=1`; a downstream law remains allowed. | `docs/MINIMAL_AXIOMS_2026-06-29.md:114-145,181-190`, registered as the canonical premise node. |
+| Convention or meta-identification | `ATTEMPTED` | Declare the Wilson and link scalars to occupy one slot. This closes bookkeeping and locates `beta=6`, but it does not provide the requested physical derivation; the bounded claim explicitly leaves this route open as convention-level handling. | `docs/G_BARE_SAME_SLOT_BETA6_CONVENTION_NOTE_2026-07-11.md:4-19,39-62`. |
+
+There are at least five normalized route families. One route remains
+constructively open and is displayed as the positive continuation, which is
+why the packet ships only the narrow current-premise sentence.
+
+## N2 — Wall-independence audit
+
+The collapsed open-condition set is:
+
+- `W_S`: sharpness, needed only to reduce the invariant effect square to the
+  nontrivial `P_3/P_1` PVM;
+- `W_U`: an update-law selector conditional on fixed sharp effects;
+- `W_N`: an independently fixed one-tick dimensionless fluctuation
+  normalization, needed to select a Wilson coefficient;
+- `W_A`: physical selection/identification of the Wilson action surface,
+  outside the supplied-action theorem.
+
+| Pair | Closing first closes second? | Closing second closes first? | Independent? |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `W_S`, `W_U` | no; sharp effects retain the `lambda` family | no; an update rule conditional on an effect need not derive sharpness | yes |
+| `W_S`, `W_N` | no; effect sharpness fixes no gauge stiffness | no; a fluctuation coefficient fixes no POVM effect | yes |
+| `W_S`, `W_A` | no; a sharp registration does not select an action | no; an action does not force a sharp effect | yes |
+| `W_U`, `W_N` | no; repeatable update selection need not fix a tick rate | no; a Hessian law need not choose a measurement update | yes |
+| `W_U`, `W_A` | no; a state-update law does not select Wilson dynamics | no; Wilson dynamics does not select the instrument | yes |
+| `W_N`, `W_A` | no; the displayed law is conditional on a named kernel and does not physically identify that kernel | no; choosing the Wilson form leaves `beta` free | yes |
+
+No wall is duplicated or downstream of another as defined. The conditional
+Wilson coefficient theorem uses `W_A` as a supplied surface and isolates
+`W_N`; it does not claim to close the full four-condition set.
+
