+## N7 — Strongest steelman
+
+A hostile reviewer should object that the coefficient family proves only that
+the predicates chosen so far are insufficient. A reflection-positive transfer
+construction tied to an independently derived Record clock could produce a
+normalised one-tick fluctuation theorem; Theorem W1 would then turn that new
+mechanism directly into `beta=2N_c`. The concrete terminal obligation is to
+derive both the tick independently of gauge diffusion and
+`-Hess_e log K_tick=g_can`, not to declare either. The approved minimal-axiom
+boundary leaves downstream dynamics open rather than forbidding it, and the
+operator-side leading-point discussion in
+`docs/WILSON_TEMPORAL_KERNEL_CASIMIR_GENERATOR_BETA_GBARE_TRANSPORT_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-07-01.md:195-199`
+points at the same route, although that row is currently unaudited.
+
+This is a convincing objection to a universal no-go. Therefore the universal
+claim is rejected. The shipped claim is demoted to the exact current-premise
+counterfamily statement, which the steelman does not contradict.
+
+## N8 — Cross-cycle echo
+
+Repository searches covered the prescribed broad phrases, all Block 54 nearby
+notes, and current open PRs.
+
+| Similar earlier wall | Later mechanism/disposition | Application here |
+|---|---|---|
+| finite-link/Wilson same-slot ambiguity | separated into exact split algebra plus a meta convention | Keep the convention route available; do not relabel it a physical derivation. |
+| gauge per-step rate dial | rate can be supplied/calibrated after a kernel class is chosen | An independently fixed tick plus fluctuation law may close `W_N`; current packet does not foreclose it. |
+| spatial/temporal kinetic-form ambiguity | owner-approved `kinetic_isotropy_primitive` registered a structural choice | Shows an explicit primitive is a possible governance mechanism, but that primitive's own boundary excludes dimensionless dynamical couplings; a new proposal would require explicit approval. |
+| prior broad `requires new axiom` walls | later operational, convention, or bounded-import reframings narrowed them | This packet says neither “requires new axiom” nor “no retained primitive”; it lists the reframe and import-retirement paths. |
+
+The same mechanisms have been considered rather than silently excluded.
+
+## Gate verdict
+
+`PASS` for the quoted narrow current-premise sentence and raw same-carrier
+boundedness obstruction. `FAIL` for any universal statement that beta cannot
+be derived, that all electric/magnetic dualities fail, or that an axiom is
+required. The source note uses only the passing scope.
